5 are negative for <italic>E. histolytica </italic>DNA; Lane-M, 100 bp DNA ladder (Bangalore genei, Bangalore).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="1471-2180-7-41-1"/></fig><table-wrap position="float" id="T1"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Comparison of result of PCR and antigen detection in liver abscess pus specimen of ALA patients.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td align="left">PCR results</td><td align="center" colspan="2">Antigen detection result (no. of specimens positive)</td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td colspan="2"><hr></hr></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td align="center"><italic>E. histolytica</italic></td><td align="center">Antigen negative</td><td align="center">Total no. of specimens</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left"><italic>E. histolytica</italic></td><td align="center">55<sup><italic>a</italic></sup></td><td align="center">35</td><td align="center">90</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Negative</td><td align="center">1</td><td align="center">21</td><td align="center">22</td></tr><tr><td align="left">Total</td><td align="center">56</td><td align="center">56</td><td align="center">112</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><p><sup><italic>a </italic></sup><italic>E. histolytica </italic>was detected by microscopy and/or culture in 10 of these 55 ELISA and PCR positive liver abscess pus specimens.</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T2"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Detection of serum antiamoebic antibody, liver pus <italic>E. histolytica </italic>antigen, liver pus <italic>Entamoeba </italic>DNA and urine <italic>Entamoeba </italic>DNA in ALA patients.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td></td><td></td><td align="center" colspan="8">No. (%) of positive results by:</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td colspan="8"><hr></hr></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td align="center">IHA for :</td><td align="center">ELISA for:</td><td align="center" colspan="5">